    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nThe builtin [:DiffTool](https://neovim.io/doc/user/plugins/#difftool) is broken when using a dir-diff when mini.files is enabled as the default explorer.\n\nThe issue goes away if i set `options = { use_as_default_explorer = false }`\n\nI get the following error, then mini.files open for the directory:\n```\nvim.schedule callback: ...vim/runtime/pack/dist/opt/nvim.difftool/lua/difftool.lua:64: Vim:E5601: Cannot close window, only floating window would remain\nstack traceback:\n        [C]: in function 'only'\n        ...vim/runtime/pack/dist/opt/nvim.difftool/lua/difftool.lua:64: in function 'setup_layout'\n        ...vim/runtime/pack/dist/opt/nvim.difftool/lua/difftool.lua:385: in function 'diff_dirs'\n        ...vim/runtime/pack/dist/opt/nvim.difftool/lua/difftool.lua:495: in function 'open'\n        .../runtime/pack/dist/opt/nvim.difftool/plugin/difftool.lua:25: in function <.../runtime/pack/dist/opt/nvim.difftool/plugin/difftool.lua:24>\n```\n\nI actually first encountered a similar issue in [fyler.nvim](https://github.com/FylerOrg/fyler.nvim/issues/358), and checked `mini.files` to see if it has a fix the issue.\n\nIt seems to me that a possible is is adding an early return for `vim.wo.diff == true` around https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/lua/mini/files.lua#L1438 , but I don't have time to test it right now :(\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Create separate 'nvim-repro' config directory:\n    - '~/.config/nvim-repro/' on Unix\n    - '~/AppData/Local/nvim-repro/' on Windows\n\n2. Inside 'nvim-repro' directory create a file named 'init.lua'.\n   Populate it with the following content:\n\n    ```lua\n    -- Clone latest 'mini.nvim' (requires Git CLI installed)\n    vim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\n    local mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\n    local clone_cmd = { 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', 'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim', mini_path }\n    vim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\n    vim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n    -- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\n    vim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim')\n    require('mini.deps').setup()\n\n    require('mini.files').setup({ options = { use_as_default_explorer = true } })\n    ```\n\n3. Run `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim` (i.e. execute `nvim` with `NVIM_APPNAME` environment variable set to \"nvim-repro\").\n   Wait for all dependencies to install.\n\n1. Follow the steps in https://neovim.io/doc/user/plugins/#difftool to add :DiffTool as your git diffing tool.\n2. Go to a git repository with changes in multiple files.\n3. Run `git difftool --dir-diff .`",
